### 6.10  Shadow Copy (Microsoft VSS)

**Shadow Copy** is a Microsoft technology (Volume Shadow Service) that creates point-in-time backup snapshots of files or volumes. It is relevant to SOC analysts primarily in the context of **ransomware response** — a common early action by ransomware payloads is to delete all shadow copies to prevent recovery:

```
vssadmin delete shadows /all /quiet
```

The presence of this command in process logs or EDR telemetry is a high-confidence indicator of ransomware execution. See [Module 5, Section 5.3](#module-5) for full post-exploitation context.

